Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: no default channel preferences

Every device's data model got three anticipated channel preferences (op
class 83 channel 6, 128 channel 42, 135 channel 7, preference 14), and
em_config's Channel Selection Request carries them. An agent that completes
the channel preference exchange then moves its radios to those channels
and widths: in the lab, off the world's 20 MHz channels 6, 36 and 37.
Channel preferences are the operator's to set; without one the request
carries none and the agent keeps its channel.

The controller stored the defaults with each device and loads them at
start: ignore those rows (exactly the three defaults) when loading.

Upstream-Status: Pending

